6. THREE LEVEL SYSTEM

A critical rule:

> The three levels do NOT represent three different component libraries.



A component family can exist across multiple levels.

The level controls things such as:

density;

scale;

height;

typography;

padding;

icon scale;

border/stroke;

radius;

spacing;

visual hierarchy.


Therefore the HTML must represent:

Component Family
 ├── Level 0
 ├── Level 1
 └── Level 2

rather than:

Level 0 components
Level 1 components
Level 2 components


